{{!--
    ui/env-managed-alert - notice for the settings pages registered through
    lib/ui-routes/settings-page.js, naming the form fields whose values come from the environment.
    Two kinds: fields the EENGINE_SETTINGS environment variable re-applies on every boot (a value
    saved for one of them holds only until the next restart), and fields whose own environment
    variable overrides the setting (lib/env-setting-overrides.js: the page shows the variable's
    value and a value typed there is not saved). Without this the page would show the save
    succeeding. Renders nothing when the page has no such field. The inputs stay enabled on
    purpose - a disabled control drops out of the POST and would silently strip its value from the
    save - so the notice is the whole treatment.
      {{> ui/env-managed-alert}}
    Reads `envManagedKeys` (array of field names) and `envOverriddenSettings` (array of
    `{key, env}`) from the page context; registerSettingsPage sets both on every render of the page.
--}}
{{#if envManagedKeys.length}}
{{#> ui/alert-banner variant="info" icon="icon-[tabler--info-circle]" title="Some fields are set by the environment"}}
<div>The following settings come from the <code>EENGINE_SETTINGS</code> environment variable and are re-applied on
    every restart. A value saved here is used until the next restart, then reverts to the environment value:
    {{#each envManagedKeys}}<code>{{this}}</code>{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}.</div>
{{/ui/alert-banner}}
{{/if}}
{{#if envOverriddenSettings.length}}
{{#> ui/alert-banner variant="info" icon="icon-[tabler--info-circle]" title="Some fields are pinned by environment variables"}}
<div>These settings are set by their own environment variable, which takes precedence over the saved setting. The
    form shows the environment value, and a value entered for them here is not saved while the variable is set:
    {{#each envOverriddenSettings}}<code>{{key}}</code> (<code>{{env}}</code>){{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}.</div>
{{/ui/alert-banner}}
{{/if}}
